---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj08.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Recognition — Fair Value at Grant Date, Expensed Over the Vesting Period" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Credit Entry — Subscription Rights to Shares (新株予約権)" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Exercise of Stock Options — Transfer to Shareholders' Equity" },
        { id: "s6", label: "THE KEY DIVERGENCE — Gain Recognition on Expiration of Unexercised Options" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Forfeiture and Vesting Conditions" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Expensing a Stock Option Grant Over the Vesting Period" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Gain on Expiration of Unexercised Options" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "J-GAAP vs IFRS 2 — Comprehensive Comparison" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Stock options as genuine compensation expense, fair-valued at grant</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 8 governs STOCK OPTIONS (ストックオプション) and other SHARE-BASED PAYMENT arrangements granted to directors, employees, and others for SERVICES rendered — establishing that such grants represent genuine COMPENSATION EXPENSE, measured at FAIR VALUE on the GRANT date and recognised over the VESTING period, rather than going UNRECOGNISED simply because no cash changes hands.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Companies granting stock options and similar equity-settled awards</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to companies granting STOCK OPTIONS (typically structured as "subscription rights to shares," 新株予約権, under the Companies Act) or other SHARE-BASED payment arrangements to directors, employees, or other parties in exchange for services.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Recognition — Fair Value at Grant Date, Expensed Over the Vesting Period</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A fixed, grant-date fair value spread across the service period</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The FAIR VALUE of a stock option grant is determined AT GRANT DATE (typically using an OPTION-PRICING model, such as Black-Scholes), and the RESULTING total compensation expense is recognised in the Statement of Income OVER the VESTING period — the period during which the RECIPIENT must provide services before the option becomes exercisable — reflecting that the option is compensation for services rendered OVER that entire period, not a single point-in-time event.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Credit Entry — Subscription Rights to Shares (新株予約権)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Building up within its own dedicated Net Assets component</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">As stock option EXPENSE is recognised, the OFFSETTING credit builds up within "SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS TO SHARES" (新株予約権) — the DISTINCT Net Assets component established by ASBJ Statement No. 5 — rather than DIRECTLY within Shareholders' Equity, since the recipient has NOT yet become an actual shareholder until the option is EXERCISED.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Exercise of Stock Options — Transfer to Shareholders' Equity</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Reclassified into Common Stock and Capital Surplus upon exercise</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">When a stock option is EXERCISED, the ACCUMULATED balance in Subscription Rights to Shares (relating to that option), TOGETHER with the exercise price PAID by the option holder, is TRANSFERRED into Common Stock and/or Capital Surplus — reflecting that the holder has NOW genuinely become a SHAREHOLDER, moving the balance INTO the ordinary Shareholders' Equity subsection.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — Gain Recognition on Expiration of Unexercised Options</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A notable, well-known departure from IFRS 2</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">If a stock option EXPIRES WITHOUT being exercised, J-GAAP requires the ACCUMULATED "Subscription Rights to Shares" balance relating to that option to be TRANSFERRED to the Statement of Income as a <strong>GAIN ON EXPIRATION OF STOCK OPTIONS</strong> (新株予約権戻入益) — typically presented as an EXTRAORDINARY or NON-OPERATING gain. This is a genuinely DISTINCTIVE, WELL-KNOWN divergence from IFRS 2, which explicitly PROHIBITS any REVERSAL of previously recognised share-based payment EXPENSE upon an equity-settled award's forfeiture or lapse due to failure to EXERCISE (as opposed to failure to VEST) — under IFRS 2, the amount SIMPLY remains WITHIN equity (often reclassified to retained earnings), WITHOUT ever flowing back through profit or loss. J-GAAP's approach of recognising a P&amp;L GAIN upon expiration is therefore a MEANINGFUL, well-recognised point of departure.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Forfeiture and Vesting Conditions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Adjusting for expected and actual forfeitures during the vesting period</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Where an employee LEAVES before an award VESTS (failing to satisfy a SERVICE condition), previously recognised compensation expense relating to that FORFEITED award is generally REVERSED — this is DISTINCT from the "expiration after vesting" scenario in Section 6, since a FORFEITURE before vesting means the award was NEVER genuinely earned, whereas EXPIRATION after vesting means the SERVICES were fully rendered but the holder simply chose NOT to exercise.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Expensing a Stock Option Grant Over the Vesting Period</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Spreading grant-date fair value across the service period</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A three-year vesting stock option grant</div><div class="wk-body">A company grants stock options to employees with a total grant-date fair value of ¥90,000,000, vesting evenly over a 3-year service period.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises COMPENSATION EXPENSE of ¥90,000,000 ÷ 3 = <strong>¥30,000,000 per year</strong>, with a CORRESPONDING credit to Subscription Rights to Shares WITHIN Net Assets each year — building up to the full ¥90,000,000 by the END of the 3-year vesting period.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Gain on Expiration of Unexercised Options</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A distinctively J-GAAP profit-and-loss consequence</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Options lapsing after the exercise window closes</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the fully-vested options (¥90,000,000 accumulated in Subscription Rights to Shares) are NEVER exercised, and EXPIRE at the end of their exercise window (e.g. because the share price never exceeded the exercise price).</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a <strong>¥90,000,000 GAIN ON EXPIRATION OF STOCK OPTIONS</strong> in the Statement of Income — a DISTINCTIVELY J-GAAP outcome; under IFRS 2, the SAME ¥90,000,000 would simply REMAIN within equity (typically reclassified to retained earnings), with NO P&amp;L gain ever recognised.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 8 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and terms of stock option and other share-based payment arrangements</span><span>Number and fair value of options outstanding, granted, exercised, forfeited, and expired</span><span>Method and assumptions used in estimating grant-date fair value</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an award has genuinely vested versus been forfeited before vesting</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Option-pricing model inputs (volatility, expected life, risk-free rate) used to determine grant-date fair value</span><span>Expected forfeiture rate during the vesting period</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>J-GAAP vs IFRS 2 — Comprehensive Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS 2</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 8)</span><span>IFRS (IFRS 2)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Grant-date fair value expensing</span><span>YES, over the vesting period</span><span>YES, over the vesting period — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Credit entry pending exercise</span><span>Subscription Rights to Shares (distinct Net Assets component)</span><span>Generally within equity (e.g. a share-based payment reserve)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Unexercised, expired options (post-vesting)</span><span>Recognised as a GAIN in the Statement of Income</span><span>Remains within EQUITY — NEVER reversed through profit or loss</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This is a genuinely NOTABLE, well-recognised divergence — the CORE grant-date fair value expensing principle is converged, but the treatment of UNEXERCISED, EXPIRED options is a MEANINGFUL point of departure between the two frameworks.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every share-based payment event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Compensation expense recognition</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> <span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Expensed over the vesting period, credited to Subscription Rights to Shares</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Exercise of options</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Transferred to Common Stock/Capital Surplus within Shareholders' Equity</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Expiration of unexercised options</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised as a gain in the Statement of Income — a J-GAAP-specific outcome</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Supplies the Subscription Rights to Shares Net Assets component this Statement's credit entries build up within</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 2</span><span>Earnings Per Share — stock options are a common source of potential dilution for diluted EPS purposes</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Stock option (ストックオプション)</div><div class="glossary-def">A right granted to a director, employee, or other party to acquire company shares at a specified price, in exchange for services.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Gain on Expiration of Stock Options (新株予約権戻入益)</div><div class="glossary-def">The J-GAAP-specific profit-and-loss gain recognised when vested stock options expire unexercised, a treatment IFRS 2 does not permit.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Vesting period</div><div class="glossary-def">The period during which a recipient must provide services before a share-based award becomes exercisable.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
